@startuml http_session_execution_controls
title HTTP Session Execution Control Design

' Source evidence (pi-mono commit 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, steer, followUp, clearQueue, and abort,
' lines 1336-1404 and 1516-1556
' packages/agent/src/agent.ts, steer, followUp, abort, and queue drain order,
' lines 275-319, 350-390, and 456-492
' packages/coding-agent/src/modes/rpc/rpc-mode.ts, steer, follow_up, and abort,
' lines 418-430
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java commit 195746614096312d4e93afb029d387837db78e0b):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/
' ChatWebSocketHandler.java, command dispatch and handleSteer, lines 199-210 and 275-288
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/
' AgentSession.java, abort and steer, lines 165-177 and 240-251
' Observed behavior: pi keeps separate steering and follow-up queues, drains steering first,
' and aborts the current in-process run. Java currently exposes text-only steer and abort.
' Java divergence: Java has no follow-up command and persists steer before actual delivery.
' Target-only design: three HTTP operations use Session scope because no public Run exists.
' Product constraint: v1 accepts text only, fixes one-at-a-time FIFO behavior, and projects
' a delivered control message as the existing durable user.message entry type.
' Design reason: separate control responses from the existing POST Events SSE response.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Credential\nAdapter" as Auth
participant "Session Control\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
collections "Active Execution\nQueues" as Queue
participant "AgentSession" as Session
participant "Existing POST Events\nSSE Stream" as SSE
participant ResultBeanFactory

group Queue a Steering Message
  Caller -> Auth : POST /sessions/{session_id}/steers\nmessage only
  Auth -> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
  API -> Store : authorize and require running Session
  Store --> API : active execution handle
  API -> Queue : append Steer atomically in FIFO order
  Queue --> API : accepted_at
  API -> ResultBeanFactory : normal(ControlAcceptedResponseVO)
  ResultBeanFactory --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
  API --> Caller : 202 Accepted
end

group Queue a FollowUp Message
  Caller -> Auth : POST /sessions/{session_id}/follow-ups\nmessage only
  Auth -> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
  API -> Store : authorize and require running Session
  Store --> API : active execution handle
  API -> Queue : append FollowUp atomically in FIFO order
  Queue --> API : accepted_at
  API -> ResultBeanFactory : normal(ControlAcceptedResponseVO)
  ResultBeanFactory --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
  API --> Caller : 202 Accepted
end

alt current Assistant turn and tools complete with Steer queued
  Session -> Queue : drain one Steer before FollowUp
  Queue --> Session : next user message
  Session -> Store : append durable user.message on delivery
  Store --> SSE : user.message with entry_id and entry_seq
  Session -> Session : continue with next model invocation
else Agent would stop and only FollowUp is queued
  Session -> Queue : drain one FollowUp
  Queue --> Session : next user message
  Session -> Store : append durable user.message on delivery
  Store --> SSE : user.message with entry_id and entry_seq
  Session -> Session : continue active execution
end

group Abort current execution idempotently
  Caller -> Auth : POST /sessions/{session_id}/abort\nno request body
  Auth -> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
  API -> Store : authorize and load Session
  Store --> API : active execution or idle
  opt execution is active
    API -> Session : abort model, tools, and subagents
    API -> Queue : clear undelivered Steer and FollowUp
    API -> Session : wait for idle
    Session --> SSE : session.status.idle
    Session --> SSE : stream.end reason aborted
  end
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content after idle
end

note over API,Queue
Steer and FollowUp require a running Session.
An idle request returns 409 SESSION_NOT_RUNNING.
Abort on an idle Session is a successful no-op.
No control id or public Run resource is created.
end note
@enduml

@startuml mate_agent_service_responsibility_boundary
title End-to-End HTTP and SSE Service Responsibilities

' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java: buildRoutes and wireServerRoutes
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatHandler.java: handleChat, wireSink, and forwardEvent
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java: getOrCreate and persistence methods
' Observed behavior: the Java baseline has an HTTP POST that returns SSE and also retains a separate WebSocket implementation.
' Target-only design: the mate-service public HTTP contract and its SSE projection are not implemented in the fixed baseline.
' Architecture change: both hops use HTTP request-response, and execution responses stream SSE for the lifetime of one execution.
' Product constraint: the UI receives chat_id only; session_id remains an internal Runtime identifier.
' Security hardening: mate-service terminates public auth and projects internal events instead of forwarding bytes transparently.
' Design reason: keep user-facing Chat lifecycle separate from durable Runtime Session identity and execution.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 18
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #334155
}

left to right direction

rectangle "Agent UI\n\nCall public HTTP operations\nUse chat_id only\nRead execution-scoped SSE\nClose on stream end or error\nNever receive session_id" as UI #EFF6FF

rectangle "mate-service\n\nOwn public HTTP and SSE\nAuthenticate the end user\nOwn Chat metadata and chat_id\nMap chat_id to session_id\nRun guardrails and orchestration\nCall CampusClaw with service identity\nProject safe public events and errors" as Mate #FFF7ED

rectangle "CampusClaw\n\nOwn internal HTTP and SSE\nAuthenticate the calling service\nOwn Runtime Session and session_id\nValidate Agent and Model\nBuild Context and execute Model and Tools\nPersist current-branch Entries\nOwn Steer, FollowUp, and Abort" as Runtime #ECFDF5

database "Mate Chat Store\n\nchat_id to session_id\nChat name and product state\nUser ownership" as MateStore

database "RuntimeSessionStore\n\nSession state and configuration\nCurrent-branch Entries\nInternal execution state" as RuntimeStore

UI <--> Mate : public HTTP requests\nResultBean, 204, or scoped SSE\nchat_id scope
Mate <--> Runtime : internal HTTP requests\nResultBean, 204, or scoped SSE\nsession_id scope
Mate --> MateStore : own and update
Runtime --> RuntimeStore : own and update

note bottom of Mate
The public and internal hops are independent contracts.
mate-service does not forward the internal stream byte for byte.
Public paths, VOs, errors, and event projection require
a separate operation-by-operation review.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Each user-message POST owns one bounded SSE response.
Steer and FollowUp are separate HTTP requests that enqueue
into the active execution. Abort is another HTTP request.
The Runtime does not read chat_id or end-user identity.
end note
@enduml

