@startuml http_session_creation
title CampusClaw HTTP Session Creation

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java: initialize
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/context/ContextFileLoader.java: loadSystemPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/skill/SkillPromptFormatter.java: format
' Observed behavior: AgentSession initialization resolves a model, loads context and skills, and creates an Agent.
' Observed behavior: initialization does not itself invoke the model or start execution.
' Target design: mate-service supplies only agent_id and CampusClaw generates session_id.
' Target design: Managed settings chooses a default candidate and Model Manager remains authoritative.
' Target design: a successful POST returns a ready SessionResource without internal version fields.
' Target design: one JWT or APPKEY adapter produces the same immutable CallerAuthContext.
' Design reason: keep Agent selection caller-visible while Runtime identity and revision stay server-owned.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "mate-service\nRuntime bridge" as Mate
participant "CredentialAuthenticationFilter" as Auth
participant "Runtime HTTP API" as API
participant "AgentDirectoryResolver" as Resolver
participant "ManagedSettingsLoader" as Settings
participant "Model Manager" as Models
participant "SessionIdGenerator" as Ids
participant "ManagedAgentSessionFactory" as Factory
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as Store
participant "ManagedSessionPool" as Pool
participant "ResultBeanFactory" as ResultFactory

Mate -> Auth : POST /agents/{agent_id}/sessions\nno request body and exactly one credential pair
Auth -> Auth : reject mixed or incomplete headers\nverify JWT or APPKEY without fallback
Auth --> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
API -> API : authorize caller\nvalidate agent_id syntax
API -> Resolver : resolve(agent_id)
Resolver -> Resolver : verify controlled root, symlinks,\nand byte-exact directory identity
Resolver --> API : agentCwd and bundle revision
API -> Settings : load(agentCwd/.campusagent/settings.json)
Settings -> Settings : verify closed fields and agentId\npin agentVersion\nvalidate enabledModels and defaultModel
Settings --> API : agentVersion, defaultModel, enabledModels
API -> Models : resolveModel(agent_id, defaultModel)
Models --> API : authoritative ModelDescriptor
API -> Ids : generate globally unique session_id
Ids --> API : session_id
API -> Factory : create immutable SessionContext\nload SYSTEM and Skills\nregister three generic tools
Factory -> Factory : construct AgentSession and Agent\nset state idle and thinking false\ndo not invoke the model
Factory --> API : ready AgentSession
API -> Store : atomically insert SessionRecord\nincluding internal agentVersion and revision
Store --> API : committed
API -> Pool : register(session_id, AgentSession)
Pool --> API : registered
API -> ResultFactory : normal(SessionCreateResponseVO)
ResultFactory --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
API --> Mate : 201 Created plus Location\nResultBean with SessionResource in result

note over API,Pool
Before commit, any failure discards the in-memory Session
and does not expose session_id.
After commit, state is idle and no MessageEntry exists.
The response contains only Session identity, current defaults,
coarse state, and creation time.
end note

note over Mate,API
This operation has no Idempotency-Key or If-Match.
Every successful POST creates a new Session.
A lost successful response can produce an orphan Session,
which background timeout cleanup must remove if unbound.
end note
@enduml

