@startuml http_delete_session
title CampusClaw HTTP Session Logical Deletion Confirmed Design

' Source evidence (pi-mono 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, AgentSession.dispose, lines 789-805
' packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/session-selector.ts,
' deleteSessionFile, lines 598-630
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java dff835743fc7f3c93e1154c3eb51028749867ca8):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java,
' remove, createSessionWithPersistence, evictIdle, and closeQuietly, lines 143-157 and 204-274
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java,
' buildCloseHook and abort command, lines 168-210
' modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/AgentSession.java, abort, lines 165-177
' Observed behavior: pi dispose stops active work and releases runtime resources, while
' interactive deletion removes the local JSONL file.
' Observed behavior: pi-mono-java SessionPool.remove only removes the in-memory entry and
' closes SessionManager; persisted JSONL can still be restored.
' Target-only design: no current pi-mono-java HTTP delete operation, durable deletion state,
' cleanup work item or tombstone implements this sequence.
' Architecture change: logical deletion and a durable cleanup work item commit atomically.
' Design reason: the API becomes idempotent immediately without exposing cleanup-job state.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Credential\nAdapter" as Auth
participant "DeleteSession\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
participant "Session Execution\nCoordinator" as Execution
participant AgentSession
participant SessionPool
participant "Cleanup\nWorker" as Worker

Caller -> Auth : DELETE /sessions/{session_id}\nexactly one credential pair, no body
Auth -> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
API -> API : validate session_id and authorize delete
API -> Store : beginLogicalDelete(session_id)

alt existing live Session
  Store -> Store : transaction: mark DELETING, reject new work,\nenqueue durable cleanup, capture execution state
  Store --> API : committed DeletePlan
  API -> Execution : block new events and configuration commands
  opt active execution exists
    API -> Execution : request abort
    Execution -> AgentSession : abort()
  end
  API -> SessionPool : remove(session_id)
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content
  Worker -> Store : claim cleanup work item
  Worker -> Execution : ensure active execution is stopped
  Execution -> AgentSession : abort() if still active
  Worker -> SessionPool : remove and release runtime objects
  Worker -> Store : purge History, internal execution state,\nand Session payload
  Store -> Store : retain session_id and deleted_at tombstone
  Worker -> Store : complete and delete cleanup work item
else missing, deleting, or deleted
  Store --> API : idempotent no-op
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content
else atomic commit failed
  Store --> API : failure, no partial deletion
  API --> Caller : 500 SESSION_DELETE_FAILED\nResultBean error without result
end

note over API,Store
Logical deletion is complete at 204.
Physical cleanup remains retryable and internal.
end note

note over Store,Worker
mate-service Chat metadata and File Service objects
are outside this operation's ownership boundary.
end note

note right of Store
The permanent tombstone has exactly two fields:
session_id and deleted_at.
Cleanup state, retries, errors, and owner data stay out.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_session_event_stream
title CampusClaw Session Event Direct POST Stream

' Source evidence (pi-mono 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/agent/src/types.ts, AgentEvent, lines 430-443
' packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts, emitToolExecutionEnd and emitToolResultMessage,
' lines 767-795
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, _handleAgentEvent, lines 781-806
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 223b6ba85d7ec80bfd4db23036fa46895294f3d0):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatHandler.java,
' forwardEvent, lines 140-160
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java,
' prompt and abort, lines 153-177
' Observed behavior: both pi baselines emit message start, update, and end events around
' one active in-memory execution. The Java HTTP handler already returns SSE from POST.
' Java divergence: the baseline aborts execution when the client cancels the SSE response.
' Target-only design: the public API persists MessageEntry records and has no public run ID.
' Architecture change: a disconnected client does not abort accepted execution; History is
' the recovery source, and replaying the side-effecting POST is forbidden.
' Design reason: preserve direct streaming while separating transient message and tool
' execution progress from authoritative User, Assistant, and ToolResult entries.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Credential\nAdapter" as Auth
participant "Session Event\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
participant "File\nService" as FileService
participant "Model\nManager" as Manager
participant AgentSession

Caller -> Auth : POST /sessions/{session_id}/events\ncredentials and user.message JSON
Auth -> API : immutable CallerAuthContext
API -> API : validate session_id and strict request body
API -> Store : load live Session and authorize event submission
Store --> API : current model, thinking, and execution state

alt another execution is active
  API --> Caller : 409 SESSION_BUSY\nJSON error without result
else Session is idle
  API -> FileService : resolve and authorize ordered file_ids
  FileService --> API : trusted file snapshots
  API -> Manager : resolve current model and input policy
  Manager --> API : authoritative model descriptor and limits
  API -> Store : persist User MessageEntry and mark active execution
  Store --> API : user entry_id and entry_seq
  API --> Caller : 200 text/event-stream
  API --> Caller : user.message\nentry_id and entry_seq
  API -> AgentSession : prompt(user message, file snapshots)

  alt execution completes
    loop each Assistant MessageEntry
      AgentSession --> API : message_start
      API --> Caller : assistant.message.started\nentry_id, no entry_seq
      loop provider increments
        AgentSession --> API : message_update
        API --> Caller : assistant.message.delta\nentry_id and typed delta
      end
      AgentSession --> API : message_end with complete message
      API -> Store : persist complete Assistant MessageEntry
      Store --> API : entry_seq
      API --> Caller : assistant.message.completed\ncomplete message and entry_seq
      opt tool calls require another model turn
        AgentSession --> API : tool_execution_start
        API --> Caller : tool.execution.started\ntool_call_id and tool_name
        AgentSession --> API : tool_execution_end
        API --> Caller : tool.execution.completed\ntool_call_id, tool_name, is_error
        AgentSession --> API : ToolResult message_start and message_end
        API -> Store : persist complete ToolResultEntry
        Store --> API : tool result entry_id and entry_seq
        API --> Caller : tool.result\ncomplete result and entry_seq
      end
    end

    AgentSession --> API : agent_end
    API -> Store : clear active execution and persist final entries
    API --> Caller : session.status.idle
    API --> Caller : stream.end\nreason completed
  else execution fails after stream start
    AgentSession --> API : execution failure
    API -> Store : retain completed entries and clear active execution
    API --> Caller : stream.error\nSESSION_EXECUTION_FAILED and localized message
    API -> API : close stream without stream.end
  end
end

note over API,Caller
Message previews and tool execution events are transient.
User, completed Assistant, and ToolResult entries are authoritative.
Session idle and stream end are non-history control events.
Stream error is a terminal non-history event and closes the response.
end note

note over Caller,Store
This POST has no application idempotency key.
After disconnect, do not replay it automatically; read History.
The accepted execution continues without the HTTP client.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_execution_resource_model
title CampusClaw Execution Resource Model Decision Record

' Source evidence verified on 2026-08-17:
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/events-and-streaming
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/sessions
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/session-operations
' https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/scheduled-deployments
' Anthropic observed behavior: user.message events drive Session work; queued events have
' processed_at=null; Session status and Session Events expose execution progress.
' Anthropic observed behavior: Deployment Run tracks Session creation success or failure,
' not the lifecycle of work inside the created Session.
' CampusClaw target evidence:
' chat-http-v1-design.md, section 2.2.1, execution resource model decision
' chat-http-v1-design.md, confirmed Session Event and execution resource decisions
' Target-only decision: neither pi baseline exposes this managed Session HTTP contract.
' Design reason: use Session Entry history as the recovery unit and avoid a redundant
' public run resource when callers only submit messages and observe Session output.
' Confirmed later on 2026-08-17: Session Events replace the earlier public Run decision.
' Architecture impact: the old active_run field was removed from CreateSession and GetSession.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 16
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
